From 9222d8407596f5cb87342be70cca6542255da60b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mat Kowalski <mko@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 01:10:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] CNO: advertise VIPs via gated redistribution, not
 static prefixes

CRD prefixes render as unconditional network statements, defeating the
kube-vip health gate: nodes with failed apiservers kept advertising the
API VIP and ECMP steered traffic into dead backends. The CR now carries
only the BGP sessions; advertisement stays with redistribute
table-direct 198 filtered to the VIP prefixes, exactly like the
bootstrap configuration.

Found during the first end-to-end BGP VIP install.
